From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: npu: do not fail NPU bind on unsupported
 TX_BUF_CHECK_ADDR

The kernel enum airoha_npu_wlan_set_cmd has 34 entries (0..33), but the NPU
firmware SET_WAIT command table has only 31 (0..30) and rejects 30..33 with
mailbox status ERROR, which airoha_npu_send_msg() translates to -EINVAL.

airoha_npu_wlan_init_memory() sends WLAN_FUNC_SET_WAIT_TX_BUF_CHECK_ADDR (32)
to publish the tx-bufid reserved-memory region.  With firmware that does not
implement it the whole sequence aborts, mt76_npu_init() returns -22 and Wi-Fi
NPU offload stays disabled while Wi-Fi itself comes up normally, so the
failure is invisible unless the error path is traced.

Treat -EINVAL from this specific command as non-fatal: firmware images that
reject it have no handler for it and never use the tx-bufid region.  Any other
error (and the errors of all remaining commands) still aborts the bind.
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c
@@ -539,8 +539,18 @@
 	if (err)
 		return err;
 
 	cmd = WLAN_FUNC_SET_WAIT_TX_BUF_CHECK_ADDR;
 	err = airoha_npu_wlan_set_reserved_memory(npu, 0, "tx-bufid", cmd);
+	/* NPU firmware images whose SET_WAIT command table holds only 31 entries
+	 * (0..30) do not implement WLAN_FUNC_SET_WAIT_TX_BUF_CHECK_ADDR (32):
+	 * they finish the mailbox transaction with status ERROR, which
+	 * airoha_npu_send_msg() reports as -EINVAL.  Those images never use the
+	 * tx-bufid region, so do not abort the whole NPU bind because of it.
+	 */
+	if (err == -EINVAL) {
+		dev_warn(npu->dev, "TX_BUF_CHECK_ADDR unsupported by NPU fw, skipping\n");
+		err = 0;
+	}
 	if (err)
 		return err;
 
